course: dictionary
lesson: 236
title: The top hunter
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An allosaurus was a dinosaur, so the word is a noun. It names a kind of animal that lived long ago. Its plural is allosauruses, when you are talking about more than one.
explain: Its name means «different lizard». Lizards are reptiles, and an allosaurus was a big reptile that walked on two legs. The name comes from scientists, so you will see it with a capital A when it is a name: Allosaurus.
explain: The word can be linked to other dinosaurs. «One bone of Allosaurus has a hole that a spike fits into exactly.» This sentence is about a spike from Stegosaurus, so it shows how scientists can match bones to find out how animals fought and lived.
fact: Allosaurus was a large meat-eating dinosaur.
fact: It walked on two legs and was about 8 to 10 metres long.
fact: It lived about 150 million years ago, in the Jurassic period.
fact: It had sharp teeth and three-fingered hands, and it was the top hunter of its time.
fact: It lived long before Tyrannosaurus rex.
exercise: Which best describes an allosaurus? | *A large meat-eating dinosaur | A type of fish found in rivers | A small plant-eating bird | A kind of cloud
exercise: Allosaurus lived about 150 million years ago. Which period was it in? | Ice Age | Victorian times | *Jurassic
exercise: What is the plural of allosaurus? | allosaurusses | allosaurus | allosaura | *allosauruses
test: How long was an allosaurus, roughly? | About 30 centimetres long | Less than one metre | About 100 metres long | *About 8 to 10 metres long
test: How long ago did allosaurus live? | About 150 thousand years ago | About 15 years ago | About 150 years ago | *About 150 million years ago
exam: Which two features did the allosaurus have? | *Sharp teeth and three-fingered hands | Feathers and a long neck | Bright paint and a horn | Wings and a beak
